WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.470
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
we got to see Patton Oswalt and Adrian Pasdar

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:11.150
on Agents of SHIELD, Garrett and Ward raided
the Fridge and learned a lot more about the

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.150
TAHITI project.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.150
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do Agents of SHIELD and bonus Marvel videos

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.250
every tuesday, be sure to subscribe to get
everything.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:23.359
My bonus video tonight is X-Men Days of Future
Past and the Apocalypse movie that’s coming

00:00:23.359 --> 00:00:24.359
next.

00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:29.140
Tonight’s episode was so awesome let’s
just get into it.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.090
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
it yet.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.119
Here’s my top 5 moments.

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:36.960
Number 5 - Garrett breaks Raina out of Prison
so she can resume Project Centipede

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.700
The whole goal of the project was to make
super soldiers.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.200
Phase 3 is basically them trying to eliminate
the threat of death.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.820
So their soldiers won’t ever die.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:50.900
There’s also a lot of tech involved and
Garrett revealed that some of his more emotional

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.500
mistakes in the past led to his cyborg parts.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.010
That’s right, they paid major homage to
the comic book version of his character, who

00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:00.309
had a bunch of his human body parts replaced
with cyborg parts.

00:01:00.309 --> 00:01:03.590
Just like Mike Peterson getting turned into
Deathlok.

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:07.150
Garrett’s cyborg parts on the show are just
less visible.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:18.950
But I wonder what kind of upgrades he’s
had?

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.710
Did anyone else get the vibe that Raina might
turn on Garrett at some point?

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:22.710
Like she’s going to be so mad that he’s
not what he claimed to be.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:25.770
She’s all about making the world better,
or whatever her idea of better is.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:29.220
And I think she sees that Garrett doesn’t
care about making anything better.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:30.810
He seems more like a thug.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:31.890
Keep your eyes on her.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.090
She might end up turning on HYDRA before the
finale.

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:37.520
Number 4 - Ward Is Everyone’s Type

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:38.880
This was so much fun.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.300
Not only was there some Ward Raina ‘shipping,
he also revealed how he got everyone on Coulson’s

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.479
team to trust him.

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:50.479
First he jumped out of the plane back in episode
6, but he started having sex with May to throw

00:01:50.479 --> 00:01:52.120
her off the scent.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:55.130
And all he had to do to fool Coulson was play
hard to get.

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:56.200
So funny.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:00.899
The promo for the next episode kind of spoiled
that Skye finds out he’s a double agent

00:02:00.899 --> 00:02:07.000
and Patton Oswalt made that huge speech to
Coulson about vetting everyone.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.110
I still think by the end of the Season he’ll
be back on Team Coulson.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.790
He kind of explained his backstory a little,
his real backstory.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:20.930
He said Garrett pulled him out of a terrible
situation.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:23.870
I think we’ll find out what that is and
because of the relationship he formed with

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:28.040
Garrett over the years, I kind of think he
got a little brainwashed.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:33.610
I think he’ll turn against Garrett eventually
and when he comes back to Team Coulson, he

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:36.459
and Skye will be just like May and Coulson.

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:37.510
Team mates, but not friends.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:42.220
Also, don’t you feel like Skye seems to
gravitate towards all the worst dudes.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:48.670
Like if I wanted to get her to go out with
me, I should join HYDRA and be evil and it

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:50.370
would just dramatically increase my chances
with her.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.780
Speaking of gravity, Number 3 - Garrett and
Ward pull Gravitonium out of the Fridge

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:59.590
The comedy of this situation is that we as
the audience know that the Gravitonium fused

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:04.340
with Franklin Hall back in episode 3.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:07.989
I think that whenever they let it out of that
box it will just cause chaos for everyone.

00:03:07.989 --> 00:03:11.560
Graviton was a villain in the comic books,
but that doesn’t necessarily mean he’ll

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:13.910
align himself with HYDRA and Garrett.

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:17.680
He might just try to destroy both Garrett
and Coulson because of what happened to him.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.290
That’s the funny thing, it always seemed
like when classic comic book heroes got super

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:25.440
powers because of some freak accident, they
were really excited about it.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:30.239
And when villains got dosed with radiation
or something else, they always sought revenge.

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:34.430
In fairness, most of the villains probably
only became evil as a result of the accidents

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:35.799
that gave them powers.

00:03:35.799 --> 00:03:37.680
Number 2 - Garrett and Ward Raid The Fridge

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.530
I actually thought this was more fun than
the Graviton reveal at the end.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:44.780
How funny was it that The Fridge is actually
on a beach?

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:46.180
They were like kids in a candy store.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:50.010
And that scene where Garrett tells Ward all
about project slingshot was so funny.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:55.290
“If it looks dangerous good, if it looks
alien great.”

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.470
My biggest question after all that was what
happened to all the monkeys they shot into

00:03:58.470 --> 00:03:59.720
space?

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:02.830
and my number 1 moment - Patton Oswalt becomes
an Agent Of SHIELD

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:07.769
I felt like he had the perfect introduction
on screen.That total nerd moment he has when

00:04:07.769 --> 00:04:09.930
he’s over explaining why the base has no
name.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:14.140
They really took it to the Nth degree with
the nerdy basement metaphor.

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:18.230
As if he’s been holed up looking at porn
and playing video games by himself in an underground

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:19.850
bunker since The Avengers.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:25.030
I’m glad to see he’s coming back in next
week’s episode and I really want to see

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:28.760
how he’s going to handle HYDRA Ward after
they find out he’s trying to get the data

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.000
on the hard drive.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.970
But let me know what you’re favorite moment
was, raiding The Fridge?

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:37.940
Raina and Garrett just dosing everyone with
mysterious blue vials of alien blood or just

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:41.610
evil Ward in general?

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:44.690
Here are couple of the bigger comic book references
I spotted in no particular order.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:48.240
There was the news report at the beginning
talking about all the leaked documents that

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.410
Black Widow released during Winter Soldier.

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:54.710
Garrett also gave her a nice shoutout when
he was complimenting Ward for infiltrating

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:56.249
Coulson’s team.

00:04:56.249 --> 00:05:01.550
The Barber Chair to the Secret Hydra base
feels like a big reference to Spies Like Us.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:06.080
When Coulson’s team talks about The Cube
being retaken, they’re talking about a Black

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.090
Site like TAHITI from the comics.

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:10.780
For a while it was used as a prison for aliens.

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:16.060
I guess you could say that blue alien in TAHITI
was also in a prison of sorts.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:19.430
When we see Glenn Talbot it’s a huge reference
to the Hulk comics.

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:23.389
He worked under General Ross, so you can imagine
how he’s going to deal with threats.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.520
Generally someone to avoid at all costs.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:29.060
And the most fun one was the Griffin reference.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:32.780
Garrett talks about the person they arrested
that had lion’s paws for hands.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:36.220
In the comics he was a normal person who had
surgery to make him look more like a mythical

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:39.610
griffin and also got dosed with a mutagenic
serum.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:45.139
Let me know if you saw any other references
I didn’t mention in the video.

00:05:45.139 --> 00:05:48.660
Overall I gave the episode a solid A, one
of the best this season.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:53.500
I think the HYDRA SHIELD in chaos plot has
really added this sense of urgency the show

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:54.500
hasn’t had.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.150
Like a ticking time bomb is still waiting
to go off.

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:59.889
I love what they did with Ward’s character.

00:05:59.889 --> 00:06:02.280
Now we know why his performance was so wooden.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:05.569
I really did not dig the Boy Scout aspect
of his character.

00:06:05.569 --> 00:06:10.040
It was like he was basing his double agent
performance based on how he thought Captain

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:12.430
America would act in similar situations.

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:17.030
Which is kind of funny when you think about
it.

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:22.819
Patton Oswalt is a giant leap forward in guest
actors, he’s so perfect for the character

00:06:22.819 --> 00:06:23.819
he’s playing.

00:06:23.819 --> 00:06:27.650
I got this meta Star Wars flashback when that
turret popped up and fired.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:31.690
Like they were on Hoth and it was the Probe
Droid Han Solo and Chewie run into.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:36.819
Which just made me think about Patton Oswalt’s
filibuster pitch for the plot of Episode 7.

00:06:36.819 --> 00:06:41.751
I’m really looking forward to the addition
of Graviton into the mix with Deathlok, Team

00:06:41.751 --> 00:06:46.340
Garrett and Team Coulson all vying for what’s
left of SHIELD.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:50.710
I’m also kind of wondering if Coulson’s
team are going to be the one’s to rebuild

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:53.800
SHIELD eventually.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:59.500
Supposedly by the time the Avengers fight
Ultron next year SHIELD will still be out

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.500
of commission.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.949
But Coulson seemed so adamant about upholding
the virtues of SHIELD.

00:07:03.949 --> 00:07:08.510
I did get pretty excited when he did that
big Agents Of Nothing Speech.

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:10.819
Let me know what you’re final thoughts are
about the episode, and let me know what you

00:07:10.819 --> 00:07:16.330
think is going to happen to Ward at the end
of the season.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:19.840
In case you missed it I just posted a breakdown
of the new X-Men Trailer you can watching

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:25.170
it by clicking here and you can check out
my Arrow Season 2 finale predictions here.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.830
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight!

